{"content":"Found the regression: in sqlparse/filters/reindent.py, `_next_token` has an inverted condition. It currently reads `if not (token and token.normalized == 'BETWEEN'):` which causes it to recursively call itself for every normal split keyword (FROM, WHERE, etc.) instead of only for the BETWEEN special-case, and it recurses even when no token was found (tidx=None), leading to `idx += 1` on None in sql.py's token_next_by. The original/correct logic only recurses into the BETWEEN handling when the found token actually is BETWEEN. I'll fix the condition and verify with reindent and the CLI.","tool_calls":[{"id":"fix_1","name":"replace_text","arguments":{"path":"sqlparse/filters/reindent.py","old_text":"        if not (token and token.normalized == 'BETWEEN'):
            tidx, token = self._next_token(tlist, tidx)

